eadings; ships new test file `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/memory_verification_retrieval.rs` per tasks.json `files_expected`.\n\nNo code was implemented; tasks.json, context.md, and plan.md were not modified."}],"totalDurationMs":848530,"totalTokens":121791,"totalToolUseCount":37,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1191,"cache_read_input_tokens":119194,"output_tokens":1405,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1191},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1405,"cache_read_input_tokens":119194,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1191,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1191,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":13,"searchCount":3,"bashCount":4,"editFileCount":17,"linesAdded":1295,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T45.log:6536:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T50.md:12:This task closes the spec's §Scope Leakage risk control: branch-scoped memory MUST NOT leak into unrelated branches, workspace-scoped memory MUST NOT leak across workspaces, and organization-scoped memory MUST NOT leak into workspaces that do not belong to that organization. The check is named verbatim in §Verification Engine's checks list. This is the source of authority for scope filtering — every retrieval, every workflow bundle, every consolidation proposal targeting a memory must obey it. Negative tests are non-negotiable: the spec's risk control names "negative tests" explicitly as part of the mitigation.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T45.log:6621:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T48.md:45:9. In `verification/existence_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) a memory whose evidence cites a live file is `Verified`, (b) deleting the file makes the next verify return `Invalidated` (assert via a proposal emitted through T39, not via a direct memory mutation), (c) a memory whose evidence cites a deleted symbol returns `Invalidated`, (d) a memory whose evidence cites a still-existing doc section returns `Verified`, (e) a memory whose evidence cites a deleted test returns `Invalidated`, (f) the `verification_jobs` schema round-trips under the migration runner against a temp DB.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T45.log:6624:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T48.md:77:- [ ] No deferred work: T49 (spans), T50 (scope), T51 (expiry + incremental), T52 (surfacing) are sibling tasks — but the eight-state output model, the existence checks, the `verification_jobs` table, and the proposal-through-T39 invariant all ship here.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T45.log:6649:docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T49.md:12:This task implements the second verification check from spec §Verification Engine: when a memory's evidence captured an exact text span (a byte range or `(start_line, end_line)`) at the time of creation, verification must confirm the current file content at that span still matches what was captured. If it does not, the verifier emits a `MarkStale` proposal (the assertion may still be true but the citation is stale) or `MarkInvalidated` (the evidence is gone). This is the difference between "the file still exists" (T48) and "what the memory said about the file is still backed by the same bytes." It is the load-bearing mechanism for the spec's §Stale Memory Leakage risk control.
